.TH DEVTOOL 1 "2026-06-20" "devtool 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
devtool \- generic unix developer helper CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devtool
.RI [ global-options ] command " [command-options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
devtool helps apply artifacts, validate repositories, summarize restore/build/test output,
copy logs to the clipboard, send notifications, and automate common repo tasks.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B restore | build | test | validate | wine-validate | run | package
Run project actions.
.TP
.B apply-overlay | apply-snapshot
Apply an artifact to a repository. Use
.BR --validate ,
.BR --validate-only ,
.BR --commit
and
.BR --commit-even-on-failure
to control optional validation and commit behavior.
.BR --skip-restore ,
.BR --skip-build
and
.BR --skip-test
can be used with
.B validate
and
.B wine-validate
to omit individual stages.
.TP
.B batch
Run a sequence of steps such as validate or apply-overlay=/path/to/file.zip.
.TP
.B config show | resolve | doctor
Inspect configuration.
.TP
.B status | doctor
Show repo and tool status.
.TP
.B logs latest
Show or print the latest saved raw log.
.TP
.B completion zsh
Print zsh completion.
.TP
.B init-config
Write a .devtool.toml template into a repo root.
.TP
.B tag | release-notes | commit
Git helper commands.
.TP
.B ai-prompt
Generate a fully resolved AI workflow prompt for the current repo.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/devtool/logs
Saved raw command logs.
.TP
.I .devtool.toml
Per-repo configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEVTOOL_PROJECT_*
Overrides [project] values from .devtool.toml.
.TP
.B DEVTOOL_ENV_*
Overrides or injects runtime env vars from [env].
.SH AUTHOR
OpenAI

.SH AI PROMPT
.TP
.B devtool ai-prompt --repo-name NAME
Print the generated prompt to standard output.
.TP
.B devtool ai-prompt --repo-name NAME --output prompt.md
Write the generated prompt to a markdown file.
.TP
.B devtool ai-prompt --project-type TYPE --build-target PATH --run-target PATH
Override detected project settings in the generated prompt.
